{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01111",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.99,
      "end_seconds": 3.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Good morning, grab a seat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.1,
      "end_seconds": 10.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "Um, you know, hello, thanks for fitting me in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.17,
      "end_seconds": 19.68,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "Okay, so doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.31,
      "end_seconds": 27.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair. So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.75,
      "end_seconds": 31.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "It's no appetite, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.19,
      "end_seconds": 40.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.1,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.29,
      "end_seconds": 57.24,
      "duration_seconds": 15.95,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, about... well, five days. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. My neighbour said I should get it looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.23,
      "end_seconds": 61.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "So, have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.37,
      "end_seconds": 92.25,
      "duration_seconds": 28.88,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a low fever as well. Mm, I've also been feeling sick, for about a week. I've also had pain that started around my belly button then moved to the right, for about a month. With pain that started around my belly button then moved to the right, mild, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.94,
      "end_seconds": 97.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.95,
      "end_seconds": 101.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 102.84,
      "end_seconds": 112.82,
      "duration_seconds": 9.98,
      "text": "Actually, uh, I remember she had some kind of reaction to tramadol before. I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.5,
      "end_seconds": 119.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Maybe, uh, but I don't recall it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.5,
      "end_seconds": 125.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.46,
      "end_seconds": 137.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Okay, tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.64,
      "end_seconds": 146.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure for five years now. I have heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.38,
      "end_seconds": 155.87,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "Alright, high blood pressure, that matches what I have here. Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.03,
      "end_seconds": 163.72,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "My mother had a stroke. Um, my aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.78,
      "end_seconds": 169.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.51,
      "end_seconds": 175.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "I, I take telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 177.51,
      "end_seconds": 181.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 20 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.51,
      "end_seconds": 187.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.58,
      "end_seconds": 197.98,
      "duration_seconds": 9.4,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day for my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 199.81,
      "end_seconds": 208.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "I mean, it's meant to be once a day, though I don't see she take it every time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.7,
      "end_seconds": 214.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.16,
      "end_seconds": 232.4,
      "duration_seconds": 16.24,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts. I hardly move around during the day. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.83,
      "end_seconds": 237.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Have you noticed diarrhoea, cough or urinary symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.56,
      "end_seconds": 244.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "Hmm, no diarrhoea, cough or urinary symptoms, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.64,
      "end_seconds": 252.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.77,
      "end_seconds": 256.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.46,
      "end_seconds": 261.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.92,
      "end_seconds": 264.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 265.9,
      "end_seconds": 275.25,
      "duration_seconds": 9.35,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temp 38.8 degrees, pulse 102, SpO2 98 percent on room air, pressure 104 over 71."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.21,
      "end_seconds": 278.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.7,
      "end_seconds": 283.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.35,
      "end_seconds": 286.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.29,
      "end_seconds": 304.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "It hurts most low on the right and it hurts when I let go of the pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.46,
      "end_seconds": 311.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "That's the examination finished."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.98,
      "end_seconds": 332.4,
      "duration_seconds": 10.42,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at possible appendicitis or a urine infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.04,
      "end_seconds": 336.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.22,
      "end_seconds": 371.23,
      "duration_seconds": 33.01,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's possible appendicitis, and we'll know more once the urgent blood tests is back. I'll request urgent blood tests, it'll help with abdominal pain. I'll request an ultrasound or CT scan, it'll help with possible appendicitis. You need to go to hospital now and not eat or drink. I'm going to send a referral to the surgical team."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.59,
      "end_seconds": 381.14,
      "duration_seconds": 8.55,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.32,
      "end_seconds": 386.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.47,
      "end_seconds": 393.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "I'd like you back straight away. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 394.5,
      "end_seconds": 399.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "Um, um, I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}